[1] user: there are a few bugs that I am frustrated with in the frontend at the moment, sessions seem to be automatically forking for some reason there is some sort of instance where messages just get lost and aren't recoverable and this is super annoying, there are  just errors if a user switches a tab or moves to a different app, the user has to keep that tab open otherwise there is an error, i honestly there should just be an option to retry a request/continue the request that got cut off. the other issue is on mobile/sm devices the settings panel is too small. also the  various artifacts are not horizontally scrollable on mobile even though i feel like they should be.

[2] user: i think adding some way for the user to tell the model about them so that they gain some understanding would be helpful. and more diversity as for the starting topics would be nice

[3] user: skip vet

[4] user: aso consider this, i think a some more things might make sense as hooks that just run on the first message in a session, the learner profile tbh should just run. it really doesn't make that much sense not to run.

[5] user: https://github.com/cactus-compute/needle would this be useful in hooks at all? i was thinking, something like a categorization/classification usecase for this model somewhere maybe  for the topics of the stuff we are asking questions on? maybe  when running some hooks. you don't have to use it but i wonder if there are some good ideas here

[6] user: what was the automatic response forking for? i was thinking that these would be options for dpo that the user would have ui to select maybe the issue wasn't the forking, the issue might have been how it was present t o the user. also would love for the text on mobile to be way more useful in term of it using more  of the screen as well.

